confirm.description:
Home Assistant will upload the packaged native agent through the currently configured maintenance API. SSH credentials are not needed. Active display and firewall patches are checked read-only first and refreshed only if they were already active and the packaged patch source changed. If you use local Ring Call handling, also verify the Home Assistant media-user setup in the integration options after the update.

Installed: {installed_version} (API {installed_api_version}, bundle {installed_bundle_hash})
Packaged: {available_version} (API {available_api_version}, bundle {available_bundle_hash})
Update path: {update_path}
Display patch status: {qml_patch_status}
Reason: {reason}

ssh_install.description:
This installed agent cannot update itself yet. Home Assistant will use these one-time SSH credentials to install the packaged agent, then refresh only active display and firewall patches when the packaged patch source changed. The SSH credentials are not stored. If you use local Ring Call handling, also verify the Home Assistant media-user setup in the integration options after the update.

Installed: {installed_version} (API {installed_api_version}, bundle {installed_bundle_hash})
Packaged: {available_version} (API {available_api_version}, bundle {available_bundle_hash})
Update path: {update_path}
Display patch status: {qml_patch_status}
Reason: {reason}

confirm.description:
Home Assistant can run the matching repair for the failed media-readiness checks now. Depending on the failed checks, this can re-check agent reachability, refresh agent setup metadata, apply the IPv4 media firewall, or repair the Home Assistant media-user/routing setup. Ring Call forwarding is never changed by this repair. IPv6 is optional and is not changed by this repair.

